    assistant: "Ang bacteria at viruses ay dalawang uri ng microorganisms na madalas na ikakamali, pero sila ay napaka-iba sa isa't isa.\n\n**BACTERIA:**\n\n**Characteristics:**\n- **Living organisms** (unicellular prokaryotes)\n- May sariling metabolism (kumakain, nag-e-excrete, nagre-reproduce)\n- Size: 0.5 - 5 micrometers (visible sa light microscope)\n- May cell structure: cell wall, cell membrane, cytoplasm, ribosomes\n- May DNA (circular, nasa cytoplasm - walang nucleus)\n- Marami ang beneficial, ilang pathogenic\n\n**Reproduction:**\n- **Binary fission** (asexual reproduction)\n- Isang cell → dalawang identical cells\n- Mabilis: E. coli ay nagdi-divide every 20 minutes sa optimal conditions\n\n**Mga halimbawa ng beneficial bacteria:**\n- **Gut flora** - Tumutulong sa digestion, gumagawa ng vitamins (K, B12)\n- **Nitrogen-fixing bacteria** (Rhizobium) - Nag-convert ng N₂ sa usable form para sa plants\n- **Decomposers** - Nagbe-break down ng dead organisms at waste\n- **Fermentation** - Paggawa ng yogurt, cheese, pickles, vinegar\n\n**Mga halimbawa ng pathogenic bacteria:**\n- **Salmonella** - Food poisoning\n- **Mycobacterium tuberculosis** - Tuberculosis\n- **Vibrio cholerae** - Cholera\n- **Streptococcus** - Strep throat, pneumonia\n\n**Treatment:**\n- **Antibiotics** - Pumatay o nagpapahinto ng bacterial growth\n- Halimbawa: Penicillin (nag-i-inhibit ng cell wall synthesis), tetracycline (nag-i-inhibit ng protein synthesis)\n- **Antibiotic resistance** - Nagiging problema dahil sa overuse at misuse ng antibiotics\n\n**VIRUSES:**\n\n**Characteristics:**\n- **Not considered living** (obligate intracellular parasites)\n- Walang sariling metabolism (hindi kumakain, hindi nag-e-excrete)\n- Hindi makapag-reproduce nang mag-isa (kailangan ng host cell)\n- Size: 20 - 300 nanometers (kailangan ng electron microscope)\n- Simple structure: Genetic material (DNA o RNA) + protein coat (capsid)\n- Ilang may lipid envelope (hal. HIV, influenza, SARS-CoV-2)\n\n**Structure:**\n- **Capsid** - Protein shell na nagpo-protekta sa genetic material\n- **Genetic material** - DNA o RNA (hindi parehong)\n- **Envelope** (sa ilang viruses) - Lipid membrane na nakuha mula sa host cell\n- **Spikes** - Proteins na nagbi-bind sa host cell receptors\n\n**Reproduction (Lytic Cycle):**\n1. **Attachment** - Virus nagbi-bind sa specific receptor sa host cell surface\n2. **Penetration** - Genetic material pumapasok sa host cell\n3. **Replication** - Host cell nafo-force na gumawa ng viral components (genetic material at proteins)\n4. **Assembly** - Viral components nag-a-assemble sa bagong virus particles\n5. **Release** - Bagong viruses lumalabas (madalas na pinapatay ang host cell)\n\n**Lysogenic Cycle (sa ilang viruses):**\n- Viral DNA nag-integrate sa host genome (provirus)\n- Nagre-replicate kasama ng host DNA\n- Pwedeng mag-activate later at pumasok sa lytic cycle\n- Halimbawa: Herpes viruses, HIV\n\n**Mga halimbawa ng viruses:**\n- **Influenza** - Trangkaso\n- **SARS-CoV-2** - COVID-19\n- **HIV** - AIDS\n- **Rabies** - Rabies\n- **Dengue virus** - Dengue fever\n- **Hepatitis viruses** - Hepatitis A, B, C\n- **HPV** - Human papillomavirus (cervical cancer, warts)\n\n**Treatment:**\n- **Antiviral drugs** - Nag-i-inhibit ng viral replication (hal. Tamiflu para sa flu, antiretrovirals para sa HIV)\n- **Vaccines** - Nag-prevent ng infection sa pamamagitan ng pag-stimulate ng immune system\n- **Walang antibiotics** - Hindi epektibo laban sa viruses (dahil walang metabolism na target)\n\n**Key Differences: Bacteria vs Viruses**\n\n| Feature | Bacteria | Viruses |\n|---------|----------|---------|\n| Living? | Oo | Hindi (considered non-living) |\n| Size | 0.5-5 μm | 20-300 nm |\n| Cell structure | Meron (prokaryotic) | Wala |\n| Metabolism | Meron | Wala |\n| Reproduction | Binary fission (independent) | Kailangan ng host cell |\n| Genetic material | DNA (circular) | DNA o RNA |\n| Treatment | Antibiotics | Antivirals, vaccines |\n| Visibility | Light microscope | Electron microscope |\n\n**Bakit importante ang distinction na ito?**\n- Antibiotics ay hindi epektibo laban sa viruses\n- Pag-inom ng antibiotics para sa viral infections (hal. trangkaso) ay:\n  - Walang epekto sa virus\n  - Nagko-contribute sa antibiotic resistance\n  - Pwedeng magkaroon ng side effects\n- Tamang diagnosis ay importante para sa tamang treatment\n\nTanong: Bakit kaya ang antibiotics ay hindi epektibo laban sa viruses? Ano ang pinagkaiba ng bacteria at viruses na nagpapaliwanag dito?"
